<!--
  The voice-session detail's avatar placeholder — head + shoulders, filled.

  Ported from `web/kit/src/lib/components/ui/icon/icons.svelte`'s
  `icon-kit-person-filled` symbol, both paths unchanged. iOS draws this one
  from the SF Symbol `person.fill`, which does not port (RULES.md); web/kit is
  the second Origon catalog that rule points at, and it carries the
  counterpart, so no asset had to be minted.

  Both subpaths declare `fill-rule="evenodd"` at source. They do not overlap, so
  the winding rule changes nothing here — it is carried over rather than
  silently dropped, since re-deriving "it happens not to matter" on the next
  edit is exactly how a glyph breaks. lint flags `fillType` as API 24+ and this
  project's floor is 23: irrelevant, because Compose parses this XML itself via
  `painterResource` (see ic_origon_logo for the measured precedent).

  Origon artwork; template-rendered — tint at the call site.
-->
